From e3c453f2afef8951812dd9794e0b228c0900c88f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:29:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] state: SessionDB schema memo keeps retrying the
 repairs it used to run on every open

Follow-up to PR #2164 (per-process `_init_schema` memo), review t_01a1d4bb379f4384 nits,
card t_01a1d4c34f905bf3.

1. Repairs the memo froze. The NULL-`active` heal (#51646; an older-build writer on the
   same store can still write NULL) ran only with the full init, so once per process per
   memo key. It is now `_heal_null_active_rows`, run by the full init and by the throttled
   per-store heal (`_run_throttled_heals`, HEAL_INTERVAL_S) on memo hits. A guarded
   duplicate-title repair that failed left the unique title index missing yet the store was
   memoized, so no open retried it until DDL or a new process; `record()` now refuses to
   memoize a store without `idx_sessions_title_unique`, so the next open reruns the init.
2. The memo key dropped `_schema_code_digest`: it was a per-process constant (hashed once
   from on-disk `hermes_state_schema.py`, possibly newer than the loaded code, skipping
   sibling migration modules) in a per-process memo, so it never distinguished anything.
   The module docstring says why no code digest is needed.
3. A heal that fails no longer waits a full interval or loses rows. The delegate-marker
   UPDATE and its trigram backfill now share a SAVEPOINT: on the autocommit writer a lock
   in `_index_healed_rows_for_trigram` after the UPDATE left healed rows out of the
   trigram index, and the next scan could not find them again. `_maybe_heal` logs an
   incomplete heal at warning and rewinds its interval claim, and a full init whose heal
   failed does not claim the interval, so the next open retries.

Tests: tests/hermes_state/test_schema_init_memo_heals.py (3 tests). RED on origin/main:
NULL-active row stays NULL on a memo hit, title index still missing after the failed
repair, failed heal leaves the marker stripped but unindexed and logs no warning. GREEN:
tests/hermes_state/ + tests/hermes_cli/test_session_recovery_lost_and_found.py,
2506 passed, 0 failed.
